  <!-- The page had a title and two controls and nothing between them: a page of switches with no
       sentence saying what turning them on does is a page somebody guesses at. -->
  <x:String x:Key="ScanSettingsDescription">AP Reelume watches your folders and adds whatever turns up in them. If watching fails or the system interrupts it, it goes back over them every so often.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ScanSettingsWatchLocal">Watch changes in local roots</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ScanSettingsFallbackMinutes">Recovery interval in minutes</x:String>
  <!-- The empty tray is the good outcome, not a blank panel: everything was identified without
       anybody being asked. IsEmpty had existed on the model all along with no view reading it. -->
  <x:String x:Key="ReviewInboxEmptyTitle">Nothing left to review</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReviewInboxEmptyDescription">AP Reelume identified everything it found without needing you. When something is unclear, it will turn up here.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReviewInboxAccessibleName">Match review inbox</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReviewInboxTitle">Review</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReassignmentSectionAccessibleName">Moved files awaiting confirmation</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReassignmentSectionTitle">Moved files</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ReassignmentSectionDescription">This file matches one that was already in the catalog. If it is the same file moved, confirm which one: it keeps its progress and your decisions under the new path. If it is a new file, say so and it stays as its own entry.</x:String>
