  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyAccessibleName">Privacy and diagnostics</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyTitle">Privacy and diagnostics</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyDescription">AP Reelume works offline. There is no telemetry, nothing is sent automatically, and diagnostics stay off until you turn them on here.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyDiagnosticsLabel">Allow a diagnostic report to be produced</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyAutoRefreshLabel">Refresh the oldest entries on their own</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyAutoRefreshDescription">When the application opens, and only if you turn this on, entries whose details are more than 90 days old are asked about again: at most 20 at a time, oldest first, and only for titles that are already identified. Never while a scan is running or a video is open.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyStatusAccessibleName">Diagnostics status</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyStatusOff">Diagnostics are off. No report is produced and none is stored.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyStatusOn">Diagnostics are on. You can see exactly what the report would contain before saving it.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyStatusExported">The report was saved in your data folder. It was not sent anywhere.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyStatusFailed">The report could not be saved. Nothing was sent anywhere.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyPreviewLabel">See what it would contain</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyExportLabel">Save the report</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyNetworkTitle">Connections this application can make</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PrivacyOfflineNotice">There is no other connection. Paths, file names, titles, your library, and your history are never sent.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="DiagnosticsPreviewAccessibleName">Report contents</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="DiagnosticsPreviewTitle">This is exactly what would be saved</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="DiagnosticsPreviewDescription">The report is this text and nothing else. You can read all of it before saving.</x:String>
