  <x:String x:Key="RootAddDuplicate">That folder is already in the library. It was not added twice and nothing was changed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="RootAddNested">That folder is inside one the library already has, or contains it. Choose one that does not overlap.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="RootAddInvalidPath">That path cannot be used as a library folder. Check that it exists and is written in full.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateAccessibleName">Updates</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateTitle">Updates</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateDescription">AP Reelume does not update itself. When you ask, it checks whether a newer version exists, tells you what changed, and installs nothing until you confirm.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateAutomaticCheckLabel">Check for new versions automatically</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusAccessibleName">Update status</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateProgressAccessibleName">Download progress</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateOfferAccessibleName">Available version</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateCheckLabel">Check now</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateDownloadLabel">Download</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateInstallLabel">Install this version</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateCancelLabel">Cancel</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateConfirmationNotice">The download is kept apart and checked before it is offered. Installing is always your decision, and your library is never touched.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusIdle">Nothing has been checked yet.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusChecking">Checking whether a newer version exists…</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusUpToDate">You already have the most recent version.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusOffered">A newer version is available. Read what changed before deciding.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusUnreachable">The question could not be asked. That does not mean you are up to date, only that nobody found out.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusUnusableRelease">A version has been published, but it cannot be used as described.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusDownloading">Downloading the newer version…</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusReady">The download is complete and verified. Nothing has been installed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusInterrupted">The download was cut off. What arrived is kept, and trying again continues from there.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusVerificationFailed">What arrived is not what the version promised. It was deleted and nothing was installed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusCancelled">Cancelled. Nothing was installed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusNotConfirmed">Nothing was confirmed, so nothing was installed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusTampered">The package had changed since it was verified. It was discarded without being installed.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusHandedToWindows">Windows is installing it. Your library stays where it is.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateStatusLaunchRefused">Windows did not open the package. Nothing was replaced. If it happens again, download the new version from the releases page and install it yourself.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedInsecureDownload">The download would not travel encrypted.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedUnusableHash">The version publishes no fingerprint to check what arrives against.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedUnsignedChecksums">The version's fingerprints are not signed by the release key, so they prove nothing about who published it.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedWrongRuntime">The package is for another architecture.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedUndeclaredSize">The version does not say how large it is, so an interrupted download could not be told from a complete one.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedIncompleteSummary">The version does not explain what changed in both languages.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="UpdateRefusedUndeclaredHost">The download would leave for a domain the privacy statement does not cover.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="MarkersEmptyTitle">No markers yet</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="MarkersEmptyDescription">Set a start and an end and save. Nothing is written to your video file.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="DetectedMarkersEmptyTitle">Nothing detected in this title</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="DetectedMarkersEmptyDescription">Either detection is off, or this file has no repeated opening to recognise.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="TracksEmptyTitle">No tracks to choose from</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="TracksEmptyDescription">This file carries a single track of each kind.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PlayerVersionsEmptyTitle">Only one version</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="PlayerVersionsEmptyDescription">There is nothing to choose between for this title.</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ShortcutsEmptyTitle">No shortcuts assigned</x:String>
  <x:String x:Key="ShortcutsEmptyDescription">The system media keys still work.</x:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
